WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.634
- So, would you be up for us
just maybe takin' a couple

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:03.467
questions
- Absolutely!

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:04.690
Yes, please!
- Okay.

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:05.910
Well, where is Ramsey?

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:06.783
Where's Ramsey?

00:00:06.783 --> 00:00:07.950
Hi!

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:09.694
- Hi, Kelly. Hi, Jessica.

00:00:09.694 --> 00:00:12.320
- What's your question?

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.770
- So, Jessica I heard that
you were in a car accident

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:18.107
and you quoted, "My
stutter started soon after

00:00:18.107 --> 00:00:20.697
"and the doctors said it
was from the head injury.

00:00:20.697 --> 00:00:22.267
"My mom said that when I stuttered

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:24.047
"it looked like my brain and I were trying

00:00:24.047 --> 00:00:26.247
"to say ten things at once."

00:00:26.247 --> 00:00:27.840
"My voice just wouldn't work."

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.950
So, from this trauma, why
did you go into singing?

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:33.760
- That, actually singing was the best way

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.460
for me to communicate.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:37.210
- I've heard about that with stutter.

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:40.040
- So I got into singing and
that was literally the way

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.130
that I could express myself

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:45.390
and how everything, like, was clear.

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:48.560
So, yeah, I don't what
caused the stuttering.

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:52.020
I mean it could've been
from the car accident,

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:52.900
something you know,

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:53.733
trauma.
- Traumatic.

00:00:53.733 --> 00:00:54.930
- Like, very traumatic.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:58.390
Other traumatic things that I
went through as a child but,

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:01.010
and I also have a million
thoughts in my head at all times.

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:02.120
- Me too.
- Like somehow

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:03.180
trying to balance that

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:04.560
I might as well just sing through it.

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:05.540
- I love that.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:06.740
I love that, great question.
(laughs)

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:08.920
So next question though
is from Ashley, right?

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:09.753
Where's Ashley at?

00:01:09.753 --> 00:01:10.790
Hi, Ashley.

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:12.110
- Hi, Kelly. Hi, Jessica.

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:13.210
So you talk about being sober

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:14.940
and you're actually just
speaking about that now,

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:15.980
what brought you to the point

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:18.270
where you felt like you had to get sober?

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:20.350
- Well, being a mother.

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:25.350
Like, I mean my kids at the
time were five and four.

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:30.380
So, I grew up with no alcohol
in the house and I was,

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:33.630
but I mean I was at a place
where I was literally like,

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:36.810
spiraling with the alcohol, like,

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:39.570
and I was missing out moments of,

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:42.430
like, missing out on
moments with my children

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:45.450
and then they were seeing me
and they were very confused

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:48.473
and I just wanted to be present

00:01:48.473 --> 00:01:52.440
and have clarity and be a good
role model for my children.

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:53.990
'Cause I've always wanted
to be a good role model

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:56.530
for the world, so why in
the world would I like,

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:58.970
be stuck in this cycle of having

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:01.790
to like wake up and have
a drink before going

00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:03.340
to one of their school assemblies.

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:04.410
It got to the point where

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:07.360
all of my life had like, escalated

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:11.630
and I couldn't suppress it and alcohol,

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:13.273
it wasn't working.

00:02:13.273 --> 00:02:15.487
It was making me just
completely check out.

